# Line-ending policy for a cross-platform (Linux + Windows) checkout.
#
# Many files here are pinned by sha256 or compared byte-for-byte (game bundles, state maps,
# event logs, golden vectors). If git's autocrlf rewrote their line endings on a Windows
# checkout, those hashes would no longer match. Force LF in the repository AND on checkout on
# every platform so the bytes are identical everywhere. This is a no-op on Linux/macOS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never subject to line-ending conversion or diffing.
*.gb       binary
*.gbc      binary
*.state    binary
*.bin      binary
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.ico      binary
*.pdf      binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.ttf      binary
*.otf      binary
